  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that metipranolol may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is reported to target DNA polymerase iota, which in turn is targeted by N-[(4R,10R,13S)-17-[1-(dimethylamino)ethyl]-4-hydroxy-10,13-dimethyl-2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-tetradecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-yl]-N,3-dimethylbut-2-enamide, a compound that ultimately targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. Additionally, metipranolol is reported to target Phosphodiesterase 6C, which is targeted by Broussoaurone A, another compound that also interacts with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings collectively indicate that metipranolol may exert its effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the inhibition or modulation of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the targeting of downstream enzymes, which in turn influence the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The strength of the evidence is moderate, as the relationships are inferred through multiple indirect pathways, and further experimental validation would be required to confirm the direct interaction between metipranolol and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex.",
